From: OmacVM
Subject: [PATCH] ui: the pointer's image with extra brightness, tested without AppKit

What: a header with no AppKit in it: the gain the pointer's image gets
(the frames' gain while extra brightness boosts them, else 1x) and the
image in half floats, extended linear sRGB, premultiplied, its colour
decoded as the frames are (omacvm_bright_linear) and times that gain.
Used by omacvm-cocoa-pointer-bright.patch (which explains the why).

Why its own file: so the rules are tested without QEMU or a window
(app/runtime/Tests/display/test-pointer-bright.sh applies this patch and
omacvm-cocoa-extra-brightness-logic.patch to an empty folder; at build
time and in CI).

Upstream: with omacvm-cocoa-pointer-bright.patch; not sent.
Test: app/runtime/Tests/display/test-pointer-bright.c.

diff --git a/ui/omacvm-pointer-bright.h b/ui/omacvm-pointer-bright.h
new file mode 100644
--- /dev/null
+++ b/ui/omacvm-pointer-bright.h
@@ -0,0 +1,57 @@
+/*
+ * OmacVM: the guest's pointer image with extra brightness (ADR 0054, 0050).
+ *
+ * No AppKit in here, so it is tested on its own
+ * (app/runtime/Tests/display/test-pointer-bright.c); ui/cocoa.m uses it.
+ *
+ * With the switch "Pointer on its own layer" QEMU's cursor layer shows the
+ * guest's pointer over its frames. With extra brightness the frames are
+ * drawn in extended linear sRGB times a gain g (up to 2x). An 8-bit image
+ * stays at 1x, so the pointer would be dimmer than the page under it. While
+ * the frames are boosted, the image gets the same g: decoded to linear
+ * light like the frames (omacvm_bright_linear) and times g.
+ *
+ * In: QEMU's cursor pixels as the 8-bit layer takes them (32 bits, bytes
+ * B G R A, alpha not premultiplied, sRGB). Out: half floats R G B A,
+ * premultiplied, extended linear sRGB; the colour times g, the alpha as it
+ * is.
+ */
+#ifndef OMACVM_POINTER_BRIGHT_H
+#define OMACVM_POINTER_BRIGHT_H
+
+#include <stdbool.h>
+#include <stddef.h>
+#include <stdint.h>
+#include "omacvm-bright.h"
+
+/*
+ * The gain for the pointer, in hundredths: g while the frames are boosted
+ * above 1x, else 1x (the plain 8-bit image).
+ */
+static inline int omacvm_pointer_gain(bool boosted, int gain_c)
+{
+    return boosted && gain_c > OMACVM_BRIGHT_ONE ? gain_c : OMACVM_BRIGHT_ONE;
+}
+
+/* n pixels from src into dst (4 half floats each), times gain_c / 100. */
+static inline void omacvm_pointer_bright_pixels(const uint32_t *src, size_t n,
+                                                int gain_c, _Float16 *dst)
+{
+    double g = gain_c / (double)OMACVM_BRIGHT_ONE;
+    double lin[256];
+
+    for (int i = 0; i < 256; i++) {
+        lin[i] = omacvm_bright_linear(i / 255.0);
+    }
+    for (size_t i = 0; i < n; i++) {
+        uint32_t p = src[i];
+        double a = (p >> 24) / 255.0;
+
+        dst[4 * i + 0] = (_Float16)(lin[(p >> 16) & 0xff] * g * a);
+        dst[4 * i + 1] = (_Float16)(lin[(p >> 8) & 0xff] * g * a);
+        dst[4 * i + 2] = (_Float16)(lin[p & 0xff] * g * a);
+        dst[4 * i + 3] = (_Float16)a;
+    }
+}
+
+#endif
